WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.390
Star Wars: The Last Jedi somehow managed to
keep pre-release details shrouded in secrecy

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:10.620
- and that caused fans to dream up their own
unusual theories and speculations before even

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:11.600
buying a ticket.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:16.180
Considering that at two and a half hours,
The Last Jedi is the longest franchise entry

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:21.000
to-date, there's a lot to look forward to
that no amount of teasers could possibly spoil.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.440
But some of the behind-the-scenes details
surrounding the movie were guarded a little

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:25.440
less under carefully.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:30.900
From Easter egg reveals to production conflicts
as well as even one or two plot-related scoops

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:35.660
that came through a little earlier than expected,
here's what you might not know about Episode

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:36.160
8.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:38.020
One last stand

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.839
Due to the unexpected passing of actress Carrie
Fisher, Princess Leia's planned appearance

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.040
in Episode 9 became a point of major speculation
for fans.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:50.780
Given that her part in the next film was supposed
to be enhanced, the loss made some fans wonder

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:55.060
whether the filmmakers might digitally insert
her into Episode 9 like they had in Rogue

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:55.560
One.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:01:00.999
Lucasfilm boss Kathleen Kennedy, however,
dispelled rumors of a potential CGI Leia appearance

00:01:00.999 --> 00:01:05.820
in Episode 9 and said The Last Jedi will mark
Princess Leia's last physical appearance in

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:07.140
the Star Wars universe.

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:12.160
Perhaps it's a fitting final stand for Fisher
because, as director Rian Johnson has since

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:15.640
revealed, she was instrumental in his script-writing
process for the picture.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:19.820
Johnson said that while developing Episode
8, he'd go to her house and talk with her

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:24.860
about the script; what resulted were "...a
kind of stream of consciousness, jazz poetry

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:29.181
sessions" and that their conversations usually
led to changes in the script, such as in the

00:01:29.181 --> 00:01:29.820
dialogue.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:34.600
Considering a large portion of Fisher's non-Star
Wars career was spent doctoring screenplays

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:39.240
like this, The Last Jedi sounds like it'll
feature a culmination of her many talents.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:41.160
Actor objections

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:45.580
It's no secret that Mark Hamill hasn't been
entirely pleased with the process of bringing

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:47.460
Star Wars back for the New Trilogy.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:52.100
First, he was disappointed over his lack of
screentime in The Force Awakens and its treatment

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:57.140
of Han Solo, and now, he's taken umbrage with
Rian Johnson's vision for The Last Jedi.

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:01.460
In an interview with Vanity Fair, Hamill said
that he confronted Johnson about his thoughts

00:02:01.469 --> 00:02:02.740
on the script, and told him,

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:06.389
"I pretty much fundamentally disagree with
every choice you've made for this character."

00:02:06.389 --> 00:02:10.880
Luckily for Johnson, though, Hamill wasn't
put off enough to walk away and instead, he

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:11.880
told the writer-director,

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:15.830
"Having said that, I have gotten it off my
chest, and my job now is to take what you've

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:18.340
created and do my best to realize your vision."

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:22.740
So even though The Last Jedi will feature
a Luke Skywalker that Luke Skywalker himself

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:26.160
doesn't approve of, at least the actor will
be giving it his best effort.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:28.180
Unique influences

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:32.879
Even if Mark Hamill doesn't quite get his
vision, Rian Johnson sure boasts some novel

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:36.100
sources of inspiration for his segment of
the Star Wars films.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:41.409
For example, the aerial dogfights and space
combat seen in The Last Jedi were at least

00:02:41.409 --> 00:02:46.780
partially inspired by 1949's Twelve O'Clock
High, an American war drama about the U.S.

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:48.880
Air Force's involvement in World War II.

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:54.220
Additionally, 1964's Three Outlaw Samurai
has impacted his directing style, meaning

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:58.750
that that movie's pulpy plot and hack-'n-slash
sword fighting action will have a presence

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:02.209
among the space drama and fancy lightsabers
of Star Wars.

00:03:02.209 --> 00:03:06.660
The film series drawing influence from classic
films is nothing new, since A New Hope borrowed

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:12.890
from 1954's The Dam Busters and Akira Kurosawa's
1958 film The Hidden Fortress, so while those

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:17.920
might not be the most ordinary muse movies,
maybe this means an even truer return to classic

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:18.780
Star Wars.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:20.700
Royal cameo

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:24.980
If you were tickled by the news that James
Bond actor Daniel Craig had a cameo in The

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:28.740
Force Awakens, well, you're in for a royal
surprise in The Last Jedi.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:31.800
"There's loads of rumors man, but you know
it's a hard secret to keep, you know the Royal

00:03:31.801 --> 00:03:33.450
Family in the, in the Star Wars universe?

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:35.060
I'm sure you wouldn't be able to keep that
secret."

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:39.740
"I know nothing"

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:44.579
Princes Harry and William were both seen on-set
goofing around, and actor John Boyega confirmed

00:03:44.579 --> 00:03:46.260
that Tom Hardy was there as well.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:47.980
Boyega said of the surprise guests,

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:48.860
"They were there.

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:50.079
I'm sick of hiding it.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:51.500
I think it was leaked, anyway.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:52.920
There were images."

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:57.500
He took it a step further in November, 2017
by telling The Hollywood Reporter that not

00:03:57.519 --> 00:04:02.040
only would both princes appear as stormtroopers
in the film — in addition to Hardy and singer

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:07.160
Gary Barlow— but they'd all donned the instantly
recognizable armor for the same scene.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:09.100
Scar switcheroo

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:14.100
When it came to Kylo Ren's gnarly facial scar,
Rian Johnson has admitted that he moved it

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:17.240
simply because it didn't look right back in
The Force Awakens.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:21.860
Now it resides on Kylo's right cheek rather
than the bridge of his nose… not because

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:25.600
of midichlorians, but just because of his
own personal preference.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:29.700
It's not exactly universe-shattering canon
reconfiguration there, but it is something

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:32.720
Kylo Ren's fans will certainly take notice
of.

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:34.260
Code name

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:39.920
Just as Return of the Jedi used the fake working
title "Blue Harvest" to fool autograph-seeking

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:43.950
fans during filming, The Last Jedi had its
own pretend moniker in play while the cameras

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:45.260
were still rolling on the film.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:50.700
But instead of holding any clues to the substance
of Episode 8, the fake name was simply "Space

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:51.200
Bear."

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.620
Yep, Space Bear.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:57.540
That might be some subtle nod to Chewbacca
or one of the other furry creatures coming

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:03.230
along in The Last Jedi, or the fact that porgs
are basically the new Ewoks … or it might

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:05.900
just be Rian Johnson toying with everyone
because he can.

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:07.280
Thanks for watching!

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.760
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:12.340
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

